s the efficient management of large volumes of documents, data, and other digital assets."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1110, "end": 1280, "text": "By condensing metadata, filing systems can quickly identify, categorize, and retrieve relevant information, reducing the time and effort required for document management."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1281, "end": 1317, "text": "**Evidence from US Patent 11356539**"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1319, "end": 1454, "text": "US Patent 11356539, granted on June 14, 2022, provides conclusive evidence of the dynamic utilization of condensing metadata in filing."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1455, "end": 1661, "text": "The patent, titled \"System and Method for Efficient Data Management,\" describes a novel approach to data management that involves the condensing of metadata to facilitate faster data retrieval and analysis."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1662, "end": 1803, "text": "According to the patent, the system uses a metadata condenser to reduce the size of metadata, making it more efficient to store and transmit."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1804, "end": 1941, "text": "The condensed metadata is then used to facilitate rapid data retrieval, enabling users to quickly locate and access relevant information."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1942, "end": 1962, "text": "**Credible Sources**"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1964, "end": 1997, "text": "* US Patent and Trademark Office."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1998, "end": 2005, "text": "(2022)."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2006, "end": 2054, "text": "System and Method for Efficient Data Management."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2055, "end": 2074, "text": "US Patent 11356539."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2075, "end": 2122, "text": "* National Archives and Records Administration."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2123, "end": 2130, "text": "(n.d.)."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2131, "end": 2150, "text": "Metadata Standards."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2151, "end": 2218, "text": "Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.archives.gov\\/records-mgmt\\/metadata>"}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2219, "end": 2268, "text": "* International Organization for Standardization."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2269, "end": 2276, "text": "(2019)."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2277, "end": 2374, "text": "ISO\\/IEC 11179-1:2019 - Information technology -- Metadata registries (MDR) -- Part 1: Framework."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2375, "end": 2435, "text": "Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.iso.org\\/standard\\/72251.html>"}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2437, "end": 2451, "text": "**Conclusion**"}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2453, "end": 2582, "text": "The dynamic utilization of condensing metadata played a significant role in the filing event, as evidenced by US Patent 11356539."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 59, "text": "Dynamic Utilization of Condensing Metadata and Royal Assent"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 61, "end": 265, "text": "The dynamic utilization of condensing metadata, a patented technology (US Patent 11356539), has been implicated in the significant event of royal assent, a formal approval of a proposed law in monarchies."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 266, "end": 288, "text": "History of Involvement"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id":